WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.897
Before moving on, make sure you can explain the reasoning behind the techniques we used.

00:00:05.897 --> 00:00:09.392
Why are null and blank text different?

00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:17.702
Because null represents the absence of an SQL value, while a blank is still a stored text value.

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:22.537
Why do we flag an invalid numeric value before correcting it?

00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:27.514
Because knowing that a value is wrong does not tell us the correct replacement.

00:00:28.126 --> 00:00:32.262
Why do we separate duplicate detection from survivor selection?

00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:38.562
Because identifying possible matches and deciding what to do with them are different decisions.

00:00:38.562 --> 00:00:41.493
What does a regular expression prove?

00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:45.068
Only that text matches the selected structure.

00:00:45.068 --> 00:00:48.922
And why test updates with returning and rollback?

00:00:48.922 --> 00:00:53.873
Because we can inspect the proposed changes before permanently keeping them.

00:00:53.873 --> 00:01:01.883
If you can explain these ideas in your own words, you understand the logic behind the SQL rather than only the syntax.
